{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"B3 test contract frozen. authoritative_contract: ticket 040e acceptance criteria plus init.py merge=ours contract; production reconcile workflow must configure merge.ours.driver=true after mounting tickets and before any merge, while canary retains rebar init and no duplicate direct config. trigger_preconditions: fresh runner-shaped clone with tickets worktree, committed .gitattributes marking .bridge_state/* merge=ours, and divergent rewrites of bindings.json. production_path: parse the checked-in workflow, execute its direct git-config command in a real clone, then merge divergent tickets history in the mounted worktree. test_tier: unit config-artifact lint for ordering/canary scope; real-git integration for merge semantics because a lower tier cannot exercise attributes, repository config, worktrees, or Git's merge driver. observable_postcondition: configured scenario merges successfully, preserves exact local JSON bytes, has no conflict markers, and leaves clean worktree; negative control without config fails ordinary text merge and writes conflict markers. collateral_invariants: canary remains unedited and derives config from rebar init; unrelated workflow ordering remains intact. ci_gate: make test; focused proofs pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py -v and pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_merge_driver.py -v. Held-out plan: implementer sees only unit happy-path test; real-git integration oracle is physically removed during dispatch. Strong coordinator retained test design because oracle spans workflow and Git semantics."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785599965471682001,"uuid":"05e3af48-db40-4813-93a5-39d7b88f2db5"}